# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- Kernel#autoload_relative (Ruby 4.1) ---
#
# Issue #1691. Ruby 4.1 adds the global function `autoload_relative`
# (`load.c`, call-seq `autoload_relative(const, filename) -> nil`), the
# top-level counterpart of `Module#autoload_relative` (`module.rbs`). No rbs
# release through 4.2 declares it, so a top-level call reported
# `call.undefined-method` on correct 4.1 code.
#
# TEMPORARY: delete this file once the rbs release Rigor bundles declares
# the method upstream.
#
# Declared unconditionally, not gated on `target_ruby` (ADR-121 § Rejected
# alternatives; false positives outrank). A global function is a private
# instance method plus a public singleton method on `Kernel` — what rbs
# spells `def self?.` — so the two halves are declared on two modules,
# one `Kernel` includes and one it extends. A later direct `def self?.`
# from rbs or a project `sig/` overrides both instead of raising
# `DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError` for the whole module (see
# `process.rbs`). The included module's self type is `BasicObject`: the
# default, `Object`, includes `Kernel` itself, and that cycle is a
# `RecursiveAncestorError` that takes `Object` and every class under it
# down to `Dynamic[top]`.
module RigorCoreOverlay
  module Ruby41KernelAutoloadRelative : BasicObject
    private

    def autoload_relative: (Symbol | string const, string | _ToPath filename) -> nil
  end

  module Ruby41KernelSingletonAutoloadRelative
    def autoload_relative: (Symbol | string const, string | _ToPath filename) -> nil
  end
end

module Kernel
  include RigorCoreOverlay::Ruby41KernelAutoloadRelative
  extend RigorCoreOverlay::Ruby41KernelSingletonAutoloadRelative
end
